WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:06.340
Anne-chan!

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.610
<b>Combined Japan 
High School Cup</b>

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.270
Thank you.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:25.750
Cool Kurusu!

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.940
Anne-chan!

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.910
Cool Kurusu!

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.010
Kurusu Anne sends it in one!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.270
She's on a mission here.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.270
How many routes will she 
send before she's satisfied?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.900
She even one-shots Problem 8, 
which nobody else has even cleared!

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.320
She's good enough to cruise through 
the prelims, but she's going all out.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.150
It's awe-inspiring.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.200
Meanwhile, Group B is on speed climbing.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.110
Here we have one of the climbers to watch,
 Hanamiya Girls' Uehara Jun.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.210
As one of the fastest 
speed climbers in Kanto,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.290
will she be able to break Kokureikan's 
stranglehold on the top spots?

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.540
On your marks.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.160
Ready.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.740
Quick!

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.180
Uehara zooms up the wall 
with astounding speed!

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.830
She clocks in at 12.10 seconds. 
That's a great time.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.460
<i>I couldn't match Kurusu Anne 
or Takahashi Mimu, huh?</i>

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.940
Even Uehara-senpai couldn't 
beat them in speed?

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.420
Troix!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.310
<i>Fast and curious!</i>

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.820
Even the cream of the crop in 
Kanto can't catch Anne-san.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.710
Anne-chan! Perfect!

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.170
Kokureikan's Kurusu Anne sends the problem!

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.470
Cool Kurusu!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.470
Anne-chan!

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:08.750
I'm going to beat you and win the 
Combined Japan High School Cup!

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.850
You what?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.990
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.240
<b><i>Wall 12   The Road to Best in Japan</i></b>

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.240
Here are the prelim results.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:28.290
#1 Kurusu Anne   Kokureikan
#2 Iwamine Chinari   Kurikawa
#3 Fujita Masumi   St. Caterno
#4 Benibana Hifumi   Kokureikan
#5 Uehara Jun   Hanamiya
#6 Takahashi Mimu   Kokureikan
#7 Kasahara Konomi   Hanamiya
#8 Kumagai Chigusa   Kurikawa
#9 Sugiura Nonoka    Hanamiya
#10 Samura Rina   St. Caterno

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.570
The following 20 climbers 
have made it to the finals.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.610
Yes! We all made it through in the top ten!

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.040
But the team rankings...

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>School      No.       Name       Total Points</b>

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>Kokureikan</b>

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>Hanamiya</b>

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>A1 Kurusu Anne

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>E2 Sugiura Nonoka

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.050
Kokureikan are way out in front.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.980
We're gonna overtake them!

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:38.590
Got it.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.640
Okay...

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.220
Konomi?

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.000
You okay?

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.970
Yeah.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.680
Let's go.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:46.890
Yeah.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.600
Whoa!

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.580
Hey!

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.350
Uchimura?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.060
You didn't have to jump out of your boots...

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.060
Can you blame her?

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.760
"This time, I will win."

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.700
"Let's meet in the finals," I said...

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.700
But we're going to have to postpone that.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.950
You'd better win!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.780
Or else you'll have hell to paw...

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.100
<i>Yeah... I gotta put in everything 
I've worked toward,</i>

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.820
<i>and make sure I leave with no regrets.</i>

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.370
Listen, Konomi.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.880
Are you okay, Anne-san?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.090
W-Well, it just feels like 
you're going harder than usual.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.090
I'm drilling it into their thick skulls.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.980
Try as they might, they'll never 
even be fit to lace my boots.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.990
Those scrub climbers will 
learn their lessons,

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:40.490
and it's gonna hit them so hard
 they'll never feel like climbing again.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.640
Oh, but you girls are fine.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.990
You're Cool Kurusu in my book.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.740
Anne-san...

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.070
Whoa!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.720
Thunderbolts and lightning−very, very 
frightening, just like these finals!

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:57.720
What?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.730
Don't mind me.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.170
Let's have Nakata-san explain how 
the competitors will be ranked.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:04.890
Sure.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.010
<i>Unlike the prelims, where a climber's 
rankings in each discipline were added up,</i>

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:13.670
<i>here they'll be multiplied and the 
smaller numbers will come out on top.</i>

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:21.530
Speed                Bouldering              Lead

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.800
<i>As you see onscreen, rather than the 
ones who are average in all three,</i>

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.460
<i>climbers who specialize in even one 
discipline will come out on top.</i>

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.530
I see.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.830
The Combined Japan High School 
Cup finals are about to begin!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.820
Climbers will compete in the 
order of speed, bouldering and lead.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:34.810
We start with speed−

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.400
Anne-chan!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.260
Wow, listen to those cheers.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.840
It's Kurusu Anne, who stands atop the 
high school girls' climbing world!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.600
In the prelims, she placed first in each 
discipline and is currently the top individual.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.600
Kokureikan are the favorites 
to win the team title.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.750
She's like a star.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.590
Not just "like." She <i>is</i> the top 
star of the climbing world.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.660
She's up against a girl who picked 
up climbing less than a year ago

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:04.300
but is already attracting major attention, 
Hanamiya Girls' Kasahara Konomi.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.490
She's a real hot prospect.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.620
Hanamiya was the second best 
team in the prelims.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.120
Oh? Kurusu is approaching Kasahara.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.130
Is this her way of showing respect 
as a pro? Such a beautiful sight!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.000
Can't catch me.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.380
You can't catch me.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.930
You'll cool, cool, cool 
your heels far behind me.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.120
Guys, give Konomi-chan 
a big Cool Kurusu, too!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.340
Cool Kurusu!

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:35.940
Listen, Konomi.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.440
Don't take Kurusu Anne's bait.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.700
You'll be fine if you 
remember how <i>you</i> climb.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.240
<i>You're right, Jun-chan.</i>

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.240
On your marks.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.990
Ready.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.500
<i>Go, go!</i>

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.260
<i>Go, go, go!</i>

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.500
<i>Go, go!</i>

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:03.840
<i>Go, go!</i>

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.000
<i>Go, go!</i>

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:06.680
<i>Go!</i>

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.340
<i>That's my personal best.</i>

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.110
<i>But...</i>

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.150
Can't touch me.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.900
Can't catch me.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.770
Can't chase me.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.530
Left in the dust!

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.280
Would you believe it? Kurusu Anne has 
posted another new personal best!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:33.740
Someone once said...

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.100
"I'm going to beat you and win the 
Combined Japan High School Cup!"

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.000
Or did I just imagine that?

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.250
Thank you, everyone!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:46.000
Anne-chan! Cool Kurusu!

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.890
Here are the speed climbing results.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.690
<b>#1  
  Kurusu Anne</b>

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.400
In first, by a country mile, Kurusu Anne!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.270
<b>#2 
Takahashi Mimu</b>

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.090
In second, another Kokureikan 
climber, Takahashi Mimu!

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.280
<b>#3 
Fujita Masumi</b>

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.930
In third, St. Caterno's Fujita 
Masumi stamps her authority!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.780
<b>#4 
 Iwamine Chinari</b>

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.560
Kurikawa's Iwamine Chinari slides 
her large frame into fourth place!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.250
<b>#5 
 Uehara Jun</b>

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:18.710
In fifth, the ever-reliable speedster, 
Hanamiya Girl's Uehara Jun.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.630
Skipped.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:25.000
<b>#10 
  Kasahara Konomi</b>

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.000
Tenth-placed Kasahara Konomi did 
her best, but she seems down!

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.670
Konomi?

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.010
Why'd I have to go and say that?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.380
What?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.140
I told Anne-san I'd beat her and win.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.520
Isn't that obvious?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.020
Because Hanamiya's gonna win. Am I wrong?

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.100
Jun-chan...

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.670
Yeah! We have to win!

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.450
I mean...

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.910
I went and declared to Sayo-chin that 
I'd lead the team to victory as vice captain.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:01.640
Uh...

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.610
You posted a personal best, right?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:09.100
Maybe you couldn't beat Anne, but you 
did your best in your worst discipline.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.840
Be proud of yourself.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.000
You and Nono-senpai were 10th and 11th. 
That's more than good enough.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.200
Yeah.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:22.000
Coming up are bouldering and lead. 
That's where you shine.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.060
Konomi.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:27.310
You scaled the wall in your way, 
and now it's our turn to scale ours.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.690
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.650
I'm gonna overcome this, too.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.030
To be best in Japan.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.660
To be best in Japan.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.280
To be best in Japan.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:49.500
<b>#1    Kurusu Anne</b>

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.680
The competition in bouldering 
was truly heated!

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:50.170
Kurusu Anne takes first place 
because she used fewer attempts!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.010
<b>#2  Iwamine Chinari</b>

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.010
In second is Iwamine Chinari, who made 
full use of her height and reach!

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:58.510
<b>#3    Fujita Masumi</b>

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.510
In third, a last of— I mean, a 
blast of tempest, Fujita Masumi!

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:02.520
<b>#4    Uehara Jun</b>

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:02.520
In fourth, Uehara Jun further 
proves she's back for real!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.520
<b>#5    Kasahara Konomi</b>

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:06.520
In fifth, another Hanamiya 
climber, Kasahara Konomi!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.480
<b>#6    Kumagai Chigusa</b>

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.480
In sixth, Kumagai Chigusa muscles in.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.030
<b>#7    Niijima Kaoru</b>

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.030
In seventh, the zombie, Niijima Kaoru.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.910
<b>#8    Sugiura Nonoka</b>

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.910
And in eighth, we have another 
Hanamiya climber, Sugiura Nonoka!

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.680
Hanamiya's on the warpath!

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.810
And now, only lead climbing remains.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.400
I can't wait to see what 
they'll show us this time.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.910
There's something in my eye...

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.610
Well, we've entered observation time.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:34.550
In lead, they'll compete on how high they 
can get within the six-minute time limit.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.380
Climbers will clip their ropes to 
carabiners set up across the route

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.160
to secure themselves while climbing.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.560
If you can clip your rope to the 
topmost carabiner, you finish.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:52.890
Too bad! No St. Caterno climbers
 could send the route!

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.050
But they did well.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.910
Kurikawa High's climbers show 
real drive and strength!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.200
But they're having a hard time finishing.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.700
Now we have Iwamine, who rose in 
the rankings after bouldering.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.980
Even she falls!

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.210
Great effort, though. She scores 32+!

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.210
Takahashi Mimu falls!

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.190
Kokureikan's climbers were steamrolling 
through everything so far,

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.220
but even Benibana Hifumi has fallen!

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.090
Lead climbing is tough!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.100
In the Combined Cup, 
stamina plays a key role.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.830
Benibana has scored 35,
 and they're currently in the lead.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.640
Anne-chan!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.900
Cool Kurusu!

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:34.120
Now, Kokureikan High's final climber 
is the Princess of Climbing, Kurusu Anne!

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.860
Listen to the crowd cheer her on!

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.050
She's had a stranglehold 
on first place so far.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.990
What kind of show will she put on for us?

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:45.880
It's said that her strongest 
asset is her stickability.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.000
Specifically, it's her 
ability to secure each hold.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:54.860
But that differs from climber to climber, 
making it highly difficult to define.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:55.550
I mean...

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.880
Okay, here we go!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.040
S-So fast!

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.390
Kurusu's going up like a rocket!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.660
Wait, she isn't just fast.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:10.060
How can she be so stable?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:14.020
Exactly. That's part of her stickability.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:16.760
Because she secures each hold perfectly,

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:20.530
she can shift her body weight precisely 
and avoid making reckless moves.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:36.290
<i>Anne-san, you can't go that fast...</i>

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.560
Isn't that...

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:41.680
Yes, it's the last hold 
Benibana could secure.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.490
She extends her arm and secures the hold!

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.390
Stickability again.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.530
It looks like a slippery hold, though.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.050
Finger and grip strength.

00:11:55.050 --> 00:12:00.780
She has the ability to turn holds that are 
barely within her reach into secure ones.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.040
Here's the most difficult part.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:03.780
A dyno!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.290
She hangs on!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.600
Impressive. But...

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.670
She's moving way too fast 
through this problem.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:28.760
Incredible. She has a perfect 
read on each and every hold.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:31.390
Oh?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.940
Kurusu has come to a halt.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.400
She's almost to the top!

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.960
<i>That hold's probably a front sloper.</i>

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.400
<i>I should go in both hands at once.</i>

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:49.770
<i>One last move.</i>

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.480
<i>The only climber to send 
this route will be me,</i>

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.420
<i>Cool Kurusu!</i>

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.680
Whoa, Kurusu falls!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.100
Her dyno fell just a little bit short.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.670
You'd expect her stickability 
to make up for that...

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:20.320
But she seemed to be going full tilt 
through speed, bouldering, and now this.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.320
Even in a high school 
competition, she goes all out.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.710
Perhaps she was trying to surpass 
her own physical limits here.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:31.080
Right. She scores 40+, which 
puts her comfortably in first.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.830
Guys!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.960
Anne-chan!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.080
Cool Kurusu!

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:44.410
Jun joined, Konomin joined,

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.840
and the Hanamiya Climbing Team
 grew so much.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.660
I'm proud of our team.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.680
We've done so well to get this far.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.160
You two can hold your heads up high.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:56.100
All that's left...

00:13:56.610 --> 00:14:00.800
is for us to give this team's founder 
and captain who was forced to withdraw,

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.310
Sayo-chin, the greatest gift of victory!

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.230
Yeah!

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.240
Good luck, Uehara-senpai!

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:11.040
Hanamiya Girls' Uehara Jun is here.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:15.250
She has placed on the podium in speed 
and bouldering competitions before,

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:19.100
but not in lead, giving the impression 
that it's not her strongest suit.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:23.740
That aside, she hadn't entered <i>any </i>
competitions in the last six months.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:27.420
After failing to send any problems 
in the Kanto Bouldering Championships,

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.750
she went into hiding for a while.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.890
<i>Watch me, Konomi.</i>

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.890
<i>I'll prove that my last six 
months weren't for nothing!</i>

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:44.510
Uehara's dazzling us all 
with her dynamic moves.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.160
Yes, she's looking good.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.650
You can't tell she took a break.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.320
She may not have entered any competitions,

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:55.160
but she must've spent these past 
six months bettering herself.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:04.110
You can really sense her inner strength.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.090
There's zero hesitation in her moves.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:11.220
After that painful experience, 
Jun regained her style of climbing

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.970
and became better than ever before.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.600
Kurusu currently holds the top spot.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.850
How far can Uehara go?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.380
She falls!

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:52.750
Too bad!

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.210
If only we could've seen her 
last a little longer.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.760
But still, she scores 36+! A great effort!

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.770
I wanted to go higher still...

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.270
Damn Uchimura.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:09.030
Next up is Hanamiya Girls' Sugiura Nonoka!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.780
Good luck, Sugiura-senpai!

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.280
Good luck, Nono.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:19.480
<i>I practiced like crazy 
with Sayo-chin for this.</i>

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.040
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:27.200
<i>It's true that tall people with long limbs
 have an advantage in climbing.</i>

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.050
<i>But even without all that,</i>

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.300
<i>there must be a way for me to compete!</i>

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.780
A pied à main really does feel amazing!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.270
Sugiura's biggest asset 
is her flexibility, huh?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.040
Yeah.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.940
You could mistake her for a gymnast up there.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:49.500
However, this route could prove 
quite stressful for a short climber.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.570
Go, Sugiura-senpai! Go!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.080
Stretch!

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.880
I'm going to work you to 
the bone again today.

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:11.880
What do you do when you a 
hold is barely out of reach?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.030
I <i>wish</i> I knew!

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.660
Don't give up. There are options.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:21.630
If you keep practicing grabbing holds 
that you think are out of reach,

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:24.640
you'll start to see your range expand.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:38.860
Yes!

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.040
Ta-dah!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.120
A-Amazing, Sugiura-senpai!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.660
Right? Nono is amazing!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:56.010
Look at this! Sugiura hangs in there!

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.120
She's showing real fight!

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.250
She just won't take no for an answer!

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.810
Nono-senpai...

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:16.320
All right!

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:20.320
Huh?

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.320
No! What a shame!

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:25.050
She falls!

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:28.360
But she scores a 40! An incredible showing!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.430
<i>Sayo-chin!</i>

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>All yours now, Konomin.</i>

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:53.770
And now we have 
Hanamiya Girls' final climber,

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.160
the new star who took the scene by storm,

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:59.490
the dark horse in this competition,
 Kasahara Konomi!

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.100
<i>I will climb this, no matter what.</i>

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.000
Good luck, Master!

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:12.750
So far, she's shown what she's capable 
of in both bouldering and speed.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:17.980
I hear Nakata-san's speed climbing 
camp paid big dividends?

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.760
Oh, I don't know about that!

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:29.270
<i>All I had in life was puzzle games.</i>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.780
<i>But then, I encountered climbing...</i>

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.770
<i>and broadened my horizons so much.</i>

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:39.280
<i>I even made friends, 
teammates who climb with me.</i>

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:42.650
<i>Whenever I messed up or got down on myself,</i>

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:47.240
<i>Captain, Nono-senpai, and Jun-chan 
dragged me out of the dumps.</i>

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:53.170
<i>It's only because they were there 
for me that I made it this far.</i>

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.760
<i>I've met an opponent who 
I couldn't beat at my best,</i>

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.550
<i>someone who was way out of my league,</i>

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>and I let her get to me, but...</i>

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:09.180
You scaled the wall in your way, 
and now it's our turn to scale ours.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.930
I'm gonna overcome this, too.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.190
You two can hold your heads up high.

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:22.070
To be best in Japan.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.830
I'm going to beat you and win the 
Combined Japan High School Cup!

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.460
<i>Hanamiya will win, I swear it!</i>

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.580
<i>Those words will not go down as a lie!</i>

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.090
Go, Master!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:36.500
She sends it!

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:54.120
<b>Individual
#1   Kurusu Anne   Kokureikan
#2   Kasahara Konomi   Hanamiya
#3   Iwamine Chinari   Kurikawa
#4   Uehara Jun   Hanamiya
#5   Fujita Masumi   St. Caterno
#6   Takahashi Mimu  Kokureikan
#7  Sugiura Nonoka  Hanamiya
#8   Benibana Hifumi   Kokureikan
#9   Kumagai Chigusa   Kurikawa
#10   Samura Rina   St. Caterno</b>

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:58.170
<b>Team
#1   Hanamiya Girls' High School
#2   Kokureikan Girls
#3   Kurikawa High
#4   St. Caterno High</b>

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:28.570
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.750
Best in Japan!
